{"step_index":284,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-04T05:38:31Z","input_tokens":2738,"cache_read_tokens":175416,"output_tokens":2038,"thinking":"I'm thinking through how to approach this.\n\n\nThe device requires a specific bypass method to enable developer mode due to a ZTE-implemented RSA-2048 challenge. Attempting to repeatedly press \"Build number\" (Compilación) is ineffective without a successful bypass. Further examination reveals that ZTE's QR code check uses `/cache/recovery/last_QR` to determine if a valid QR code has been previously scanned.\n\n\nAnalysis indicates a critical bypass method: pre-baking a specific value into the `cache_ext4.img` file. This value, `\"EE@\"`, injected into `/cache/recovery/last_QR`, disables the QR code check. This approach bypasses the need for repeated attempts to scan a QR code by pre-authorizing the device with 15 unlocks.\n\n\nThe focus shifts to an external hardware bypass. Resetting the device while a USB drive is inserted allows bypassing Android and the lock screen altogether. This can lead directly to WorldCup/ADNL mode, which bypasses the usual Android interfaces, or to the Recovery menu, where entering fastboot is possible.\n\n\nThe new program bypasses the typical \"Build number\" tap requirement and enters Multi-Capture Auto Mode. It monitors for specific device identifiers (`VID_1B8E`, `PID_4EE7`, `PID_0D02`, `PID_4EE2`) associated with various boot states. Based on the detected state, the program automatically executes a sequence of commands to disable the watchdog, unlock the bootloader, enable OTG device functionality, and then transition the device into fastboot mode.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"edit_file","args":{"Path":"\"c:\\\\Users\\\\andre\\\\OneDrive\\\\Desktop\\\\xview\\\\.agents\\\\rules\\\\REGLA_SIN_ABRIR_TORNILLOS_NO_TTL.md\"","Replacement":"\"3. **Protección de claves únicas:**\\n   - Jamás flashear `factory.img` (claves DRM Widevine L1) ni `cri_data.img` (MAC y Número de Serie).\\n\\n4. **Prohibido pedir o mencionar el paso de `Configuración → Preferencias del dispositivo → Información → Compilación (presionar OK 7 veces)`:**\\n   - En las cajas Megacable Xview+ (`ZTE ZXV10 B866V2`, `MarketCode 4301`), ese paso está bloqueado por el reto RSA-2048 / Código QR de ZTE (`com.zte.adb` / `libencryCode.so`).\\n   - **No es viable y es inútil** si no se cuenta con un generador de código QR válido o si no se salta esa parte mediante los programas/métodos externos (salto por botón externo `RESET` a Recovery `fastbootd` `PID_4EE7`, U-Boot Fastboot `PID_0D02`, modo WorldCup/ADNL `VID_1B8E`, llave `QADEBUG.ini`, o inyección de `/cache/recovery/last_QR` = `\\\"EE@\\\"`).\\n   - Nunca menciones ni instruyas al usuario a hacer clic 7 veces en `Compilación`.\"","Target":"\"3. **Protección de claves únicas:**\\n   - Jamás flashear `factory.img` (claves DRM Widevine L1) ni `cri_data.img` (MAC y Número de Serie).\""}}]}
