{"step_index":292,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-04T05:39:56Z","input_tokens":2684,"cache_read_tokens":180295,"output_tokens":11229,"thinking":"Rebuilding the scripts from scratch, removing all references to the \"Compilación\" step. This necessitates a complete redesign to achieve the desired functionality without the problematic compilation component. The goal is a clean, efficient script that avoids the previous issue entirely.\n\n\nInitial concern centers on how the system handles multi-channel monitoring in `PID_4EE1` (MTP) with a USB drive. The system actively monitors four external jump channels every 200ms. Examining channel A, the recovery menu jump is triggered by USB presence and external reset, capturing `PID_4EE7` (fastbootd) to bypass the device into the bootloader, disabling the watchdog, unlocking the bootloader, and enabling `otg_device=1` for Android 12 flashing.\n\n\nAnalysis reveals three distinct jump scenarios for system access. The first uses a reset trigger with power-on, executing commands to disable watchdog, unlock the bootloader, enable USB OTG, and enter fastboot. The second immediately jumps to U-Boot fastboot mode, executing similar unlocking and flashing commands, protecting specific image files. The final path leverages ADB, installing and removing specific applications, and injecting a token.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"Content":"\"# ==============================================================================\\n# MOTOR PRINCIPAL: PROGRAMA PERFECTO XVIEW+ (ZTE ZXV10 B866V2 - S905X2 G12A)\\n# Fusion integral de todas las herramientas de la memoria USB + hallazgos REA\\n# Reglas absolutas:\\n#   1. 100% Externo (Cero tornillos, Cero TTL)\\n#   2. Proteccion total de factory.img (Widevine L1) y cri_data.img (MAC/Serie)\\n#   3. Salto directo del bloqueo QR RSA-2048 de ZTE mediante programas integrados\\n#      (Recovery fastbootd PID_4EE7 / U-Boot Fastboot PID_0D