{"step_index":300,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-04T05:47:51Z","input_tokens":200171,"cache_read_tokens":0,"output_tokens":936,"thinking":"The screenshot shows the \"watchdog off\" command executed successfully via fastboot after running \"Opción 1\". This confirms that Opción 1 successfully enters fastboot mode and that the \"watchdog off\" command is being received and executed. This behavior is consistent with the desired outcome.\n\n\nThe \"watchdog off\" and \"flashing unlock_critical\" commands executed successfully. The subsequent failures (\"locked device\") suggest an issue with device unlocking or environment variables. The \"locked device\" error persists after attempting to unlock the device and modify environment variables. It appears the device remains locked.\n\n\nThe \"locked device\" error persists despite attempts to unlock, suggesting a fundamental locking mechanism is preventing modification. The contrast between successful `watchdog off` and `erase cache` commands versus the failures on `setenv` and flashing commands points to a nuanced lock. Investigating the bootloader or previous reports for further insights into the locking behavior is warranted.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"$inf = Get-ChildItem \\\"C:\\\\Users\\\\andre\\\\OneDrive\\\\Desktop\\\\xview\\\\experimento\\\\14_MONITOREO_EN_VIVO_SMARTTY\\\\INFORME_*\\\"\\nif ($inf) { Get-Content $inf.FullName }\\n\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"5000","toolSummary":"\"Read Fastboot & U-Boot reverse engineering report\""}}]}
{"step_index":301,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-04T05:48:24Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-03T23:48:24-06:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-03T23:48:27-06:00\nCommand exited with code 0.\n\nCommand output:\n# Informe Forense en Vivo: Entrada a Fastboot, DiagnÃ³stico de `watchdog_reboot` (`U-Boot 2015.01-g220e992`) y SoluciÃ³n Anti-Watchdog\r\n\r\n**Fecha de Captura:** 29 de Octubre de 2026  \r\n**Dispositivo Analizado:** `ZTE ZXV10 B866V2` (`SN: Z41220090388172`, `MAC: C4:74:1E:F6:BE:19`, `ProductID: 48100499007041200000C4741EF6BE19`)  \r\n**SoC / Bootloader:** `Amlogic G12A (S905X2) Rev E (28:E - 40:2)` â€” `U-Boot 2015.01-g220e992 (Sep 05 2023 - 04:13:01)`  \r\n**Interfaz UART:** `Silicon Labs CP210x USB to UART Bridge (COM8 @ 115200 bps)`  \r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 1. CronologÃ­a Exacta de los 5 Reinicios Capturados en Vivo (`boot times 0` a `boot times 4`)\r\n\r\nMediante el monitor de memoria en tiempo real ([`monitor_smartty.ps1`](./monitor_smartty.ps1)) sobre `SmarTTY.exe` (`PID 3284`), se reconstruyÃ³ la secuencia completa sin desconectar el puerto serie:\r\n\r\n| Ciclo (`BL2`) | RazÃ³n de Reinicio (`BL31` / `U-Boot`) | QuÃ© OcurriÃ³ Exactamente en Hardware y Firmware | Resultado |\r\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\r\n| **`boot times 0`** | `reboot_mode=cold_boot` | Encendido en frÃ­o con el botÃ³n de Reset presionado (`GPIOAO_3 == 0`). El kernel detecta `gpio_keypad_down_cnt: 60` y ejecuta `Restarting system with command 'recovery'`. | Entra a modo **Recovery** |\r\n| **`boot times 1`** | `bl31 reboot reason: 0xd` / `0x2` (`reboot_mode:::: update`) | U-Boot lee `[commannd:boot-recovery]` en la particiÃ³n `misc`, desactiva Dolby (`recovery mode, need disable dolby`) y levanta la consola root `#` en UART. | Consola root `#` activa en Recovery |\r\n| **`boot times 2`** | `bl31 reboot reason: 0x7` (`reboot_mode:::: fastboot`) | Desde la consola root `#` se ejecutÃ³ `reboot bootloader`. U-Boot registra el gadget USB Fastboot (`g_dnl_register: g_dnl_driver.name = usb_dnl_fastboot`). Se lanza el script `.bat`: `cb_oem_cmd()` falla en `f_fastboot.c:1649` y acto seguido ejecuta `cmd cb_reboot is reboot-boot\n<truncated 3303 bytes>\n0f0d0.watchdog`)** expira y reinicia la placa (`reboot_mode=watchdog_reboot`).\r\n* Ese reinicio de hardware **borra el registro volÃ¡til `bl31 reboot reason: 0x7`** (`fastboot`).\r\n* En el siguiente arranque, U-Boot ve `reboot_mode=watchdog_reboot`, comprueba la particiÃ³n `misc` con `bcb uboot-command` (que ignora `bootonce-bootloader`), intenta leer `boot-recovery` de `misc` (`read boot-recovery from misc failed.`) y termina forzando **`ztebsp: bootcmd=bootsys`** (sistema Android normal).\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 3. SoluciÃ³n Implementada en 3 Capas (Aciertos y Mejoras)\r\n\r\n1. **Capa 1 â€” Ancla Persistente en `/dev/block/misc` desde Recovery (`#`) antes de ir a Fastboot:**\r\n   Ejecutar en `SmarTTY` (consola root `#` de Recovery):\r\n   ```sh\r\n   echo -n \"boot-recovery\" > /dev/block/misc ; sync ; reboot bootloader\r\n   ```\r\n   * **Efecto:** El registro de hardware `BL31` (`0x7`) mete la placa inmediatamente a **Fastboot**. Pero si el Watchdog llega a disparar `watchdog_reboot`, U-Boot encuentra `boot-recovery` en `misc`, **bloquea `ztebsp: bootcmd=bootsys`** y regresa siempre a la consola root `#` de **Recovery**.\r\n2. **Capa 2 â€” Enganche Inmediato `< 200 ms` sin `timeout` en [`FLASHEAR_B866V2_ANDROID12_SEGURO_SIN_PERDER_WIDEVINE.bat`](../11_VALIDACION_OTA_Y_FIRMWARE_ZTE/FLASHEAR_B866V2_ANDROID12_SEGURO_SIN_PERDER_WIDEVINE.bat):**\r\n   * Se eliminÃ³ la pausa interactiva posterior y todos los `timeout /t 2` / `timeout /t 4`.\r\n   * El script valida primero el firmware y entra en un bucle rÃ¡pido `:WAIT_FASTBOOT` que detecta la enumeraciÃ³n USB de `usb_dnl_fastboot` al instante, enviando `fastboot getvar version` y `fastboot oem \"watchdog off\"`.\r\n3. **Capa 3 â€” Retenedor Keep-Alive Indefinido ([`RETENER_FASTBOOT_ANTI_WATCHDOG.bat`](./RETENER_FASTBOOT_ANTI_WATCHDOG.bat)):**\r\n   * EnvÃ­a pulsos `fastboot getvar version` cada 2 segundos y `fastboot oem \"watchdog off\"` para mantener activa la mÃ¡quina de estados USB de `f_fastboot.c` todo el tiempo que se requiera sin que el Watchdog reinicie la placa.\r\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
{"step_index":302,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-04T05:48:27Z","input_tokens":202654,"cache_read_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1161,"thinking":"The screenshot shows the device in Recovery `fastbootd` mode, not U-Boot Fastboot. This changes the entire diagnosis. The earlier assumption about U-Boot being the active mode is incorrect.\n\n\nThe script likely didn't trigger the U-Boot sequence because the device was already in fastbootd mode, or the check failed. The screenshot reveals the root cause: the device is locked, resulting in \"remote: 'locked device'\" errors during fastboot operations. This lock status explains why the script didn't proceed as expected, since it would fail at the first command, which also indicates the bootloader is locked.\n\n\nThe exact error message \"FAILED (remote: 'locked device')\" does not originate from U-Boot 2015.01; the error string is different in U-Boot. The string is produced by Android 12's `fastbootd`, which is userspace fastboot in recovery. Android 12 `fastbootd` does not support `oem` commands or `flashing unlock` due to the locked state.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"$uboot = [System.IO.File]::ReadAllBytes(\\\"C:\\\\Users\\\\andre\\\\OneDrive\\\\Desktop\\\\xview\\\\FIRMWARE_COMPLETO_B866V2_FASTBOOT\\\\bootloader.img\\\")\\n$uAscii = [System.Text.Encoding]::ASCII.GetString($uboot)\\nWrite-Host \\\"=== Strings in bootloader.img matching 'locked' or 'unlock' ===\\\" -ForegroundColor Cyan\\n[regex]::Matches($uAscii, \\\"[\\\\x20-\\\\x7E]{4,80}\\\") | ForEach-Object { $_.Value } | Where-Object { $_ -match \\\"locked|unlock|setenv|watchdog\\\" } | Select-Object -Unique\\n\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"5000","toolSummary":"\"Check fastboot lock/unlock strings in bootloader.img\""}}]}
